  "why_safe": [
    "gdsc.c:103-117 gdsc_poll_status() reads the status register WHILE the domain is transitioning, so the GDSC status register is readable with the domain collapsed.",
    "A GDSC cannot house the registers that control its own power and clock gating; the GPUCC register file sits on always-on PMIC rails (vdd_cx pm8998_s9, vdd_mx pm8998_s6) not on the GDSC it controls.",
    "gpucc-sdm845.c:153-159 regmap is 32-bit/stride-4/max 0x8008 fast_io; gpu_cc_sdm845_probe() takes no GCC clock handle, so GPUCC register access needs no gated clock in DT.",
    "The three registers a read-only probe needs (CX status 0x05091540, GX status 0x05091010, CX control/gdscr 0x0509106c) all fall inside the GPUCC window 0x05090000+0x9000.",
    "CX status is NOT at its dtb reg 0x0509106c: gpu_cx_gdsc sets .gds_hw_ctrl = 0x1540, and gdsc.c:68-69 prefers that over gdscr, so the readable status register is 0x05091540."
  ],
  "still_unsafe_without_device_evidence": [
    "No device has read these registers yet; all values are derived from sha-pinned Linux v6.12 source plus the board DTB.",
    "Whether XNU's early boot leaves the PMIC rails voted on for GPUCC is not established; a real read must be attempted only with an explicit boot-arg gate and a watchdog.",
    "GX power-on is gdsc_gx_do_nothing_enable: writing SW_COLLAPSE cannot bring GX up, so a GX OFF result is expected even during normal runtime."
  ]
}
